FFMPEG-MUSIC

One ffmpeg invocation, run once.

RULES

1. One ffmpeg process per piece. The command text is the score.
2. Sound is made inside the invocation: expressions, generators, video sources,
   and transformations of them.
3. Any non-audio file may be read as sound. Recordings may not.
4. Codec, bitrate, bitstream filter and container choices are part of the score.
5. Playback is not composition.

FILES

NNN/pieces/NNN-slug.sh: a comment header, then one ffmpeg command ending in
"$@".

- scripts/render.sh [-f] [paths] → NNN/out/NNN-slug.{mp3,png,stats,log}
- scripts/play.sh [-l] [-s sec] [NNN | NNN | sketches | path]
- NNN/TRACKLIST: album order for scripts/play.sh NNN.
- scripts/browse.sh
- devenv shell pins the ffmpeg build.
